Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear INLA experts,
I would like to ask whether we can apply the model specified below using INLA approach and if possible some guide on the way forward.​

I have a model y_t=a*cos(w*t) + b*sin (w*t)=r*cos(w*t + m)
where r^2 = a^2 + b^2 and cos(w)=a/r
the constant r is the amplitude of the series, m the phase, w the frequency and k=2*pi/w the wavelength. The model parameters are useful in evaluating phenology metrics. Given that this is done on yearly basis using monthly composites,  I thought the model parameters should be time invariant.

I came accross this paper here (http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0167947311003999) where INLA was extended to fit such models with section 4 involving seasonal dynamic model with harmonics but a and b parameters appear to be varrying with time which should not in my case.

Test pixel time series records is attached.

 Any help and/or suggestion will be appreciated.

 Thanks in advance for your assistance.

Erick.

