On Tue, 2015-09-22 at 15:33 +0300, Erick Okuto wrote:
> Dear all,
> The time series model here is a compromise given the high spatial
> dimension  of the record (5km by 5km for Africa). I would be grateful
> if there is a way this can be solved in the spatial context with
> simplicity including amplitude+phase as model covariates.

1) As Elias wrote, it's cos-amplitude and sin-amplitude that is the
parameterisation inla can do, not amplitude and phase.
2) Do you have variables that covary with the different seasonal
pattern shapes that you can use (i.e. a parameteric model)?  Otherwise
there is no way to have the model vary spatially, unless you introduce
an actual spatial model (i.e. a nonparametric model).  That model does
not at all have to operate on the same scale as the data, but can use
large scale basis functions.
3) If all you are modelling is the seasonal pattern, then the few
cos&sin functions is the only temporal part of the model; the
coefficients can be spatial.  Then the combined effect _is_ a spatio
-temporal model, even if it's a simple one.

Finn

