Dear all,
The model only involve the seasonal temporal pattern and as you pointed out the few cos&sin functions are the only temporal part. It will be great if at least the coefficients can vary spatially in a simple way.

So inla can do cos-amplitude and sin-amplitude, do you have an idea how for example cos-phase and sin-phase can be adjusted for even by augmentation?

Do you know of some relevant documentations that can be helpful on how this is implemented in the spatio-temporal setting outlined in 3 above?

Ideally, amplitude and phase  would be expected to vary spatially and as such should be adjusted for however simple the spatial dependence structure may be.

Thanks,
Erick.

