On 22/09/15 15:47, Erick Okuto wrote:
> Do you know of some relevant documentations that can be helpful on how
> this is implemented in the spatio-temporal setting outlined in 3 above?

you can define a varying coefficients model in INLA considering that the
function f() used to define the latent model consider a second argument
that can be the covariate. Then, the index set is for the model
structure over the coefficients.
   f(index, weight, ...)
For SPDE models it is a bit trick as the model is at nodes and (usually)
the covariates are measured only at the locations. I have an example for
that and I will include it in the draft tutorial.

Elias

