Erick,

I'm not entirely sure about what you want. As I understood, I guess that
there are some issues in your code:
  - you don't need
    weight <- w*month
since later you use amplitude.cos and amplitude.sine as the weights in
f(). Isn't two models for this too much?
  - you can't have two or more f() using same index vector
  - to have dynamic model with SPDE you need to account for the fact
that the model is in a different place: at mesh nodes and time knots and
you need a trick to copy the model for the coefficients to the
covariates. On this, please consider the latest version of the draft
spde tutorial at http://www.r-inla.org/examples/tutorials/spde-tutorial

Elias

